      "title": "Chemistry – Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Chemistry – Adjunct Faculty.  SUMMARY Seeking adjunct faculty to teach various Chemistry courses and/or labs on campus in Spring Arbor. Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would seek to integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept, Statement of Faith, and Community Covenant. Applicants must be thoroughly supportive of the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian University affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. Spring Arbor University is located in Spring Arbor, Michigan. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Master’s degree in Chemistry or master’s degree in a closely related area with 18 credit hours in Chemistry. Doctorate in Chemistry is preferred. Record of successful college teaching is preferred. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839e7cf165ae017d387b34277d6b": {
      "title": "Clinical Nursing Instructor, Undergraduate - Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Clinical Nursing Instructor, Undergraduate - Adjunct Faculty.  Adjunct Clinical Nursing Instructor - Undergraduate SUMMARY This is an adjunct position responsible for teaching, supervising, and evaluating nursing students in affiliated clinical organizations, Skills Lab, and Simulation Center. The clinical instructor is an extension of the lead course faculty and supports student learning by connecting theory principles with clinical judgment. Demonstration of Competent Nursing Practice Accountable to follow the accepted standards, laws, and rules regulating the practice of nursing, and function within the scope of nursing practice. Responsible and accountable for practice based on, and limited to, the scope of instructor’s education, demonstrated competence, and nursing experience. Obtains instruction, supervision, and consultation as necessary before implementing new or unfamiliar techniques or practices. Responsible for maintaining current knowledge in broad and/or specialized areas of nursing. Conducts nursing practice without discrimination. Clinical Site Responsibilities Familiarizes self with agency policies and procedures. Completes all required agency training including, but not limited to electronic health records, HIPAA, medication administration and orientation to the unit(s) prior to taking students. Orients staff nurses to the level of the student and the specific learning outcomes for their clinical experience. Encourages communication between facility staff and faculty. Initiates regular communication with facility and unit management. Meets with patients before clinical, coordinates with charge nurse, assigns students to patients. Holds pre- and post- clinical sessions with students each shift. Department of Nursing Responsibilities Meets with lead course faculty at the beginning of each semester to orient to the course and review student learning outcomes, course syllabus, evaluation and learning resources. Participates in ongoing communication with lead course faculty and discuss instructional issues and individual student learning needs and progress. Confirms student assignments and congruence with theory content. Reviews course grading policies and Nursing Faculty Handbook. Provides feedback about adequacy of site in allowing students to meet course outcomes to the lead course faculty. Works in cooperation with the Simulation Center Coordinator when necessary. Performs tasks as assigned by the lead course faculty. Demonstrates behaviors and attitudes that are supportive Spring Arbor Nursing’s students and mission, philosophy, program goals, policies, and professional/Christian values. Serves as a professional role model and representative of the nursing department at Spring Arbor University. Student Instruction Responsibilities Directs, instructs, and guides students in the clinical setting. Assigns students to selected patients based on student’s learning needs and patient assessment. Facilitates students in comprehensive, individualized instruction in the observation, assessment, decision-making, and health teaching of patients, including the maintenance of patient health or prevention of illness or disease. Guides development of student’s critical thinking, technical, and professional communication skills while maintaining patient and student safety and patient confidentiality. Supervises the administration of medications. Delegates selected nursing functions to students in accordance with their level of nursing education and demonstrated competency. Manages students in situations of injury or illness in the clinical setting. Directs students to be responsible and accountable for their behaviors in the clinical setting. Grades written assignments, maintain accurate records, and return graded work to students in a timely manner prior to their next clinical. Completes clinical documentation as directed by the department. Maintains confidentiality HIPPA and adheres to FERPA privacy policies. REPORTING RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as a member of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences reporting to the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) Program Director as well as collaborates with the lead course faculty. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES The Adjunct Clinical Instructor will supervise students in affiliated clinical organizations. the Skills Lab, and Simulation Center. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee is frequently required to sit and use hands to finger, handle, or feel. The employee is occasionally required to stand and walk, reach with hands and arms. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 10 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, and ability to adjust focus. QUALIFICATIONS A Baccalaureate Degree in Nursing required; A Master’s Degree in Nursing is preferred. Will consider BSN degree with clinical experience of at least 2-4 years. A current unencumbered license to practice as a registered nurse in the state of Michigan. Criminal history and background check clearance, evidence of current American Heart Association CPR training, and a current unencumbered Michigan RN license. Provide evidence of yearly tuberculin skin tests and other required immunizations as per nursing program policy. Possess thorough knowledge of patient medications, treatments, and diagnoses, and has the ability to relate these aspects of patient care to problem solving/critical thinking skill development in the student. Has the ability to deal appropriately with delicate student situations, and able to effectively communicate and negotiate resolutions with faculty, students, and facility staff regarding problems in the clinical setting(s). Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the SAU Concept and Community Covenant. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Job Type Part Time Location Spring Arbor Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839f91e3131c019210ab88ad4f59": {
      "title": "Nursing - Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Nursing - Adjunct Faculty.  SUMMARY Seeking adjunct faculty to teach various undergraduate Nursing courses on campus in Spring Arbor, MI. Particular needs include OB, Pediatrics, Community Health, Mental Health, and Research. Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would seek to integrate the Christian faith into teaching Nursing and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Faculty must exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept, Statement of Faith, and Community Covenant, as well as be thoroughly supportive of the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian University affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Applicants must have a minimum of a Master’s degree in Nursing, or have a masters degree plus a bachelor’s degree in Nursing. Nursing faculty must hold a current unrestricted license as an RN in Michigan. A record of successful college teaching and experience is preferred. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883c6718f9d9a017199627e290241": {
      "title": "Online Nurse Practitioner Program - Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Online Nurse Practitioner Program - Adjunct Faculty.  Adjunct Faculty - Online Nurse Practitioner Program Job Description SAU's Online Nurse Practitioner (NP) Program is growing, and we are currently accepting applications for Adjunct FNP Faculty positions. We are looking to expand our team with dedicated Nurse Practitioners who are passionate about sharing their background and experience with our students. We are currently accepting applications from Nurse Practitioners licensed to practice in the following states: Minnesota, Nebraska, North Dakota, Oklahoma, Washington state and Wisconsin. We are also accepting applications for those licensed in Michigan who live within driving distance of main campus to assist with NP residencies. When required by State Boards of Nursing, applicants must also be prepared to secure an active, unencumbered RN and APRN license in the State of Michigan before any employment offer. Every day, nurses are directly impacting the lives of countless people, and this opportunity will allow you to share your faith, background, education, experience, and insights with tomorrow’s nurses. Experienced nurse practitioners bridge the gap between theory and practice by educating and mentoring MSN and Post-Master’s Certificate (PMC) students in a supportive, close-knit learning environment. Our Nursing Faculty brings coursework to life through both online instruction and clinical rotations. The online classroom—whether via Zoom or the Brightspace Learning Management System—serves as a vital space for connection and engagement. To ensure each student’s success, faculty maintain open communication, often reaching out proactively to provide guidance and support. Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would seek to integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. Applicants must support of the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian university affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. Spring Arbor University is located in Spring Arbor, Michigan. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE DNP or Ph.D. preferred. Master of Science in Nursing. Holds a current and unencumbered licensure in one of the 50 states (MN, NE, ND, OK, WA, and Wisconsin is preferred) as a Registered Nurse and as a Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) At least one year of experience as a certified FNP in a primary care clinical setting. Prior instructional and precepting experience with graduate-level students is strongly preferred Comfortable with the online environment, including but not limited to the Brightspace Learning Management system (preferred), ZOOM, iHuman, etc. Experience working in multicultural academic environments is preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859f889839b50188d53e97903ddc": {
      "title": "Physics – Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Physics – Adjunct Faculty.  SUMMARY Seeking adjunct faculty to teach various Physics courses and/or labs on campus in Spring Arbor. Assignments for courses in future semesters available Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would seek to integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept, Statement of Faith, and Community Covenant. Applicants must be thoroughly supportive of the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian University affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. Spring Arbor University is located in Spring Arbor, Michigan. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Master’s degree in Physics or master’s degree in a closely related area with 18 credit hours related to Physics or Applied Physics. Doctorate in Physics is preferred. Record of successful college teaching is preferred. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7885a8766d9a3c0176cdb8f9fb4962": {
      "title": "Psychiatric Mental Health NP - Online Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Psychiatric Mental Health NP - Online Adjunct Faculty.  Psych Mental Health NP – Online Adjunct Faculty SAU’s Online Psych Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Program is growing, and we are currently accepting applications for Adjunct PMHNP Faculty positions. We are looking to expand our team with dedicated PMHNPs who are passionate about sharing their background and experience with our students. We are currently accepting applications from PMHNP licensed to practice in the following states: Minnesota, Nebraska, North Dakota, Oklahoma, South Dakota, Washington, Washington, D.C., and Wisconsin. When required by State Boards of Nursing, applicants must also be prepared to secure an active, unencumbered RN and APRN license in the State of Michigan before any employment offer. Every day, nurses directly affect the lives of countless people. This opportunity will allow you to share your faith, background, education, experience, and insights with tomorrow’s nurses. Experienced nurse practitioners bridge the gap between theory and practice by educating and mentoring MSN and Post-Master’s Certificate (PMC) students in a supportive, close-knit learning environment. Our Nursing Faculty brings coursework to life through both online instruction and psych clinical rotations. The online classroom, whether via Zoom or the Brightspace Learning Management System, serves as a vital space for connection and engagement. To ensure each student’s success, faculty maintain open communication, often reaching out proactively to provide guidance and support. Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would seek to integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. The individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. Applicants must support the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian university affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. Spring Arbor University is located in Spring Arbor, Michigan. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE DNP or Ph.D. preferred. Master of Science in Nursing. Holds a current and unencumbered licensure in one of the 50 states (MN, NE, ND, OK, SD, WA, Washington DC, and Wisconsin is preferred) as a Registered Nurse and as a Psych Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (FNP) At least one year of experience as a certified FNP in a primary care clinical setting. Prior instructional and precepting experience with graduate-level students is strongly preferred Comfortable with the online environment, including but not limited to the Brightspace Learning Management system (preferred), ZOOM, iHuman, etc. Experience working in multicultural academic environments is preferred, and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a0fdaba00570ec": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Recruiting Coordinator – Baseball",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Recruiting Coordinator – Baseball.  Assistant Coach, Recruiting Coordinator – Baseball Summary Spring Arbor University is seeking a highly organized, relational, and mission-minded individual to serve as the part-time Assistant Recruiting Coordinator for Baseball. This position will support the Head Baseball Coach and baseball staff in the recruitment and enrollment of prospective student-athletes while contributing to the overall growth and success of the baseball program. The Assistant Recruiting Coordinator will play an important role in identifying and communicating with prospective student-athletes, maintaining recruiting records, coordinating recruiting activities, and helping create a positive experience for prospective student-athletes and their families throughout the recruiting process. This individual should demonstrate a strong commitment to Spring Arbor University's mission and values, possess excellent communication and organizational skills, and be able to work effectively in a fast-paced collegiate athletics environment. Essential Responsibilities Assist the Head Baseball Coach and coaching staff with all aspects of the baseball recruiting process. Identify and research prospective student-athletes who may be a strong fit for Spring Arbor University and the baseball program. Assist with maintaining and organizing the baseball program's recruiting database and prospect lists. Communicate regularly with prospective student-athletes and their families through phone calls, text messages, email, and other appropriate forms of communication. Assist with recruiting correspondence and follow-up to prospective student-athletes. Coordinate and assist with campus visits, game visits, recruiting events, camps, and other recruiting activities. Help provide prospective student-athletes and their families with information regarding Spring Arbor University, the baseball program, academics, campus life, and the admissions process. Work collaboratively with Admissions and other campus offices to help prospective student-athletes navigate the enrollment process. Assist with recruiting evaluations, research, and tracking of prospective student-athletes. Maintain accurate and timely recruiting records and documentation. Assist with the organization and execution of baseball camps and clinics as assigned. Support the baseball coaching staff with various administrative and program-related responsibilities. Represent Spring Arbor University and the baseball program professionally and positively in all recruiting interactions. Comply with all NCAA, NAIA, Crossroads League, Spring Arbor University, and Department of Athletics policies and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Baseball Coach or Director of Athletics. Qualifications Required: Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. Strong organizational and administrative skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to build positive relationships with prospective student-athletes, families, coaches, and campus personnel. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail. Commitment to the mission and Christ-centered values of Spring Arbor University. Preferred: Collegiate athletics or baseball recruiting experience. Coaching or playing experience at the collegiate level. Experience using recruiting databases, CRM systems, or other recruiting technology. Familiarity with NCAA/NAIA recruiting regulations and collegiate athletics operations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with a wide range of individuals. Ability to establish and maintain strong relationships with prospective student-athletes and families. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a coaching staff. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and other common technology platforms. Ability to represent Spring Arbor University and its mission with professionalism and integrity. Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and occasional travel as required by recruiting activities and the baseball schedule. Faith and Mission Commitment Spring Arbor University is a Christ-centered institution committed to integrating faith and learning in all areas of the university experience. The Assistant Recruiting Coordinator is expected to support the mission of the University and contribute to a baseball program that seeks to develop student-athletes academically, athletically, personally, and spiritually. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to serving and developing young men and helping create a program culture that reflects the values and mission of Spring Arbor University. Working Conditions This position may require evening and weekend work, travel for recruiting purposes, and attendance at baseball games, camps, showcases, tournaments, and other recruiting events. The position requires flexibility based on the seasonal demands of the baseball program. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859fa064222601a06dad7c2773e3": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Education",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Education.  Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Full-Time Tenure-Track Faculty Spring Arbor University is seeking an individual with teaching experience who is passionate about preparing students to impact the world for Jesus Christ within the vocation of PK-12 Education. The position will begin in January 2027. Review of applicants will begin Sept 21 and continue until the position is filled. Ideally, the new faculty member would start in January 2027. POSITION DESCRIPTION Teach a full-time (24 semester hour) load of Education courses annually, with a focus on elementary education. The successful candidate will have experience in public education and be familiar with state standards for the preparation of classroom teachers, as well as knowledge of contemporary research and evidence-based best practices in science and/or math curriculum, instruction, and assessment. The candidate should be enthusiastic about teaching and contributing to the department through advising/mentoring students, various activities related to teacher education, and working collegially with fellow faculty to support the elementary education. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE PhD or EdD in Elementary Education or a related area is strongly preferred; master’s degree in Education, Science Education, Educational Leadership, or a related area is required. The terminal degree is required for tenure-track status to be granted. Experience as a certified elementary teacher with at least five years of successful professional teaching in K-12 schools is required, with additional years of experience in teaching or K-12 leadership preferred. State Licensure in Michigan or another state is required. Successful college teaching experience in both traditional campus environments and online is preferred, as is experience with CAEP or other national education accreditation. QUALIFICATIONS Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept, the Statement of Faith, and the Community Covenant. SALARY and BENEFITS: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. Spring Arbor University provides a significant benefit package, which includes medical and life insurance and contribution to a retirement program. Experience working in multicultural academic environments is preferred, and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7885ac9c2fd15c019c3463e52f24f0": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Electrical Engineering, Dept. Chair",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor of Electrical Engineering, Dept. Chair.  Department Chair, Electrical Engineering Associate or Full Professor of Electrical Engineering Full-Time Tenure-Track Faculty Spring Arbor University is seeking an individual with teaching and administrative experience to continue to build our undergraduate Engineering program. The position will begin in the fall of 2026. POSITION DESCRIPTION The School of Engineering at Spring Arbor University (SAU) invites applicants for a tenure-track position in the field of Electrical Engineering with potential appointment as the Department Chair of Electrical Engineering. SAU offers BS degrees in Electrical and Mechanical Engineering. Teaching duties include core engineering courses and upper division courses in the candidate’s area of specialization. Responsibilities include teaching at the undergraduate level, development of scholarly endeavors, innovative curriculum development, advising students, and serving on university committees. Individuals with specializations in Electrical manufacturing, Radar and communications systems, and Power generation are especially encouraged to apply. QUALIFICATIONS Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Female candidates and candidates from diverse populations, or who have experiences working with diverse populations, are encouraged to apply. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Mission Statement, Statement of Faith, and Community Covenant. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE Applicants should have a PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or a closely related field. Previous academic administrative experience is a plus. Professional experience in the field of electrical engineering is also preferred, as is a successful record of teaching and mentoring undergraduate students. We are seeking individuals who are passionate about academic excellence and about preparing students to impact the world for Jesus Christ within the vocation of engineering. Spring Arbor University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is located on a beautiful campus in south central Michigan. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and will continue until the position is filled. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78879e9eb34c2a019ebccd51ce76f0": {
      "title": "Associate, or Full Professor of Mechanical Engineering, Dept. Chair",
      "description": "Associate, or Full Professor of Mechanical Engineering, Dept. Chair.  Department Chair, Mechanical Engineering Associate or Full Professor of Mechanical Engineering Full-Time Tenure-Track Faculty Spring Arbor University is seeking an individual with teaching and administrative experience to continue to build our undergraduate Engineering program. POSITION DESCRIPTION The School of Engineering at Spring Arbor University (SAU) invites applicants for a tenure-track position in the field of Mechanical Engineering with potential appointment as the Department Chair of Mechanical Engineering. SAU offers BS degrees in Electrical and Mechanical Engineering. Teaching duties include core engineering courses and upper division courses in the candidate’s area of specialization. Responsibilities include teaching at the undergraduate level, development of scholarly endeavors, innovative curriculum development, advising students, and serving on university committees. Individuals with specializations in Engineering Design, Thermo-fluid sciences, or Materials are especially encouraged to apply. QUALIFICATIONS Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world. The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty. Female candidates and candidates from diverse populations, or who have experiences working with diverse populations, are encouraged to apply. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Mission Statement, Statement of Faith, and Community Covenant. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE Applicants should have a PhD degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field. Previous academic administrative experience is a plus. Professional experience in the field of mechanical engineering is also preferred, as is a successful record of teaching and mentoring undergraduate students. We are seeking individuals who are passionate about academic excellence and about preparing students to impact the world for Jesus Christ within the vocation of engineering. Spring Arbor University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is located on a beautiful campus in south central Michigan. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and will continue until the position is filled. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
