    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859e9d4aea68019d8c03f4de5650": {
      "title": "Dean of the School of Nursing, Health, and Sciences",
      "description": "Dean of the School of Nursing, Health, and Sciences.  Dean of the School of Nursing, Health, and Sciences Spring Arbor University seeks its next Dean of the School of Nursing, Health, and Sciences. The Dean will provide strategic direction and oversight of academic programs, faculty, accreditation and compliance, student outcomes, operational effectiveness, and external partnerships, while exercising fiscal stewardship of the School’s resources, including budgeting, allocation, and long-term financial planning. In addition to serving as the chief nursing officer, the Dean oversees the science and health programs. Through the School’s mixture of undergraduate and graduate programs, offered online and on campus, over 800 students annually are transformed by its impact. Potential for growth is strong and will be enhanced by the remodeling and expansion of the Whiteman-Gibbs Science Center, which is underway. The Dean reports to the Provost and will have their office on Spring Arbor’s beautiful campus in south central Michigan. The School and the University are missionally focused and fiscally strong. SAU’s Concept (mission) statement has provided clear guidance to the university community since the 1960s and is hard-wired into the culture. It reads, “Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world.” The Dean will be able to articulate how the Christian faith and the Biblical worldview provide the foundation for learning for the nursing, health, and science disciplines. The individual will exhibit a life and service consistent with the University Concept and Community Covenant and must be fully supportive of the University’s mission and values as an evangelical Christian institution affiliated with the Free Methodist Church. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE Earned doctoral degree in nursing or a related discipline is required. Master’s degree in nursing or a health-related discipline is required. Leadership experience overseeing faculty, academic programs, curriculum, and accreditation and compliance. A record of successful teaching in higher education is required, with experience in teaching face-to-face and online strongly preferred. Unencumbered Michigan RN license or willing to obtain. Strong leadership and strategic planning skills. An entrepreneurial spirit and an all-institutional perspective. Experience with program development and ongoing improvement. Ability to manage multiple priorities and complex initiatives. Proven sound judgment, attention to detail, and professional integrity. Evidence of scholarship, professional service, and engagement in their academic discipline. The review of candidates will begin April 24 and will continue until the position is filled, with the new Dean in place preferably before Fall 2026. Applications are required and are available Interested individuals should submit a cover letter, statement of faith, vitae, and an application. Please contact SAU’s Provost, Dr. Carol Green, for more information about the position, or SAU’s HR office for general questions. Experience working in multicultural academic environments is preferred. Individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839fa1559acc01a15e696f746514": {
      "title": "DevOps & Infrastructure Engineer - Level I",
      "description": "DevOps & Infrastructure Engineer - Level I.  DevOps & Infrastructure Engineer - Level I Summary The DevOps Engineer supports and enhances SAU’s networking and server infrastructure, cloud solutions and software delivery through configuration management, device management, (CI/CD) pipelines, and cloud platform administration. This position ensures systems are robust, scalable, and secure while fostering collaboration between enterprise services and operations teams. The DevOps & Infrastructure Engineer also participates in optimizing IT delivery, supports security initiatives, cost optimization and high availability of services. Position is in-person on the campus of Spring Arbor University. Key Duties: Incident Management - Provide incident response support for cloud application issues and troubleshoot production issues. Escalate incidents as necessary. Identify, troubleshoot and correct applications issues to maintain high availability of services. Reinforces SLAs to manage end-user expectations. Security - Maintain effective security controls and analyze current security requirements to reduce SAU security posture. Analyze current security requirements and make suggestions for improvements toward the goal of a zero-trust model. Documentation- Develop and maintain design, configuration items, and troubleshooting documentation and develop and document procedures and best practices. CI/CD Pipeline Management Develop, maintain, and optimize CI/CD pipelines (e.g., Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI). Support build/test automation and continuous delivery practices. Cloud Platform Management Deploy, manage, and optimize cloud environments (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP and Oracle), Monitor resource utilization and implement auto scaling and cost-control strategies. Monitoring & Incident Response - Implement system monitoring, alerting, and logging using various tools. Participate in incident resolution and post-incident reviews to improve system reliability. Security & Compliance Implement DevSecOps best practices including secrets management, access controls, and compliance monitoring. Ensure secure configuration of CI/CD pipelines, API Keys, containers, and infrastructure. Project Management, Collaboration and Infrastructure Support Assists in defining software development project plans, including scoping, scheduling, and implementation. Collaborates with other stakeholders in conceptualizing and developing and updating effective applications and applications. Enterprise Solution Support Support / Incident Management- Provide incident response support for break-fix issues and troubleshoot production issues. Escalate incidents as necessary. Identify, troubleshoot and correct applications issues to maintain high availability of services. Reinforces SLAs to manage end-user expectations and train SAU-IT Helpdesk to manage tier I and II service requests. Provide problem management reviews when necessary. Solution Maintenance - Be accountable for identification, implementation, testing and maintenance for cloud based solutions and on-prem applications and hosts. System Integrations - Manage data integrations between platforms and system; includes identity integration, data mapping between external systems, data flows, data quality and monitoring. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support system integration and connectivity needs. Security - Enforce security policies and procedures to protect application gateways (web, APIs) and data between systems. Documentation and Knowledge Management - Create and maintain documents that describe the processes, procedures, systems, and knowledge needed to support Other Duties & Work Conditions May be required to work some night and weekend hours to support upgrades or resolve an outage. On-call availability to support escalated incidents. Performs other duties as assigned to meet service objectives within IT. Reporting Responsibilities Reports to the Chief Information Officer. Required: Knowledge, Skills & Abilities To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. Proficiency in delivering customer service and working with non-technical users to resolve technical issues. Technical problem-solving skills and possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Docker: Proficient in containerization techniques, including creating and managing Docker images, optimizing Dockerfiles, and orchestrating containers to ensure consistent environments across development and production. Proxmox : Demonstrate a functional understanding of open-source server virtualization management, including the deployment and maintenance of virtual machines and containers, high-availability clustering, and integrated storage and network configuration to support Spring Arbor University's infrastructure. Artificial Intelligence Analytic skills for using spreadsheets to track issues, plan projects and perform a cost analysis. Baseline understanding of using AI for technical augmentation. Knowledge and working proficiency with one of the following programming languages: Java, Python, JavaScript, NodeJS, C# or GO. Working knowledge of cloud based services (AWS, Oracle, Azure, or Google Cloud). Exercises judgment based on an understanding of organizational policies and activities. Baseline Linux/Unix skills. Baseline knowledge of SQL. Strong technical aptitude and ability to research & solve complex issues independently. Desired: Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience with troubleshooting principles, methodologies, and issue resolution techniques. Solid working knowledge of current Internet technologies, including HTML, HTTP, REST. Web development experience. Working knowledge of TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VLANs, routing protocols and VPN technologies. Hands-on experience developing test cases and test plans. SQL Relational database experience. Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field or related work experience as a Dev-Ops. Work experience will be considered in lieu of a degree. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is our moral and legal obligation to meet the responsibility of ensuring that all management practices regarding employees are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the 1964 Civil Rights Act, and other applicable federal and state statutes, all recruiting, hiring, training, and promoting for all job classifications will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military veteran status or other applicable status protected by law, including state of employment protected classes. It is, therefore, our policy and intention to evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. All personnel related activities such as compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions and privileges of employment will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military veteran status or other applicable status protected by law, including all applicable state of employment protected classes. Spring Arbor University is a Christian religious-affiliated organization; and as such, is not subject to religious discrimination requirements; the University’s hiring practices and EEO discrimination practices are in full compliance with both federal and state law. Federal law creates an exception to the “religion” component of the employment discrimination laws for religious organizations (including educational institutions) and permits them to give employment practice preference to members of their own religious beliefs. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883c6718f9d9a017199719ff50261": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Applicant Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Applicant Pool.  Adjunct Faculty - Applicant Pool This posting is intended to establish and maintain a pool of qualified adjunct faculty candidates for future teaching opportunities. While applications submitted through this pool will be retained for consideration as needs arise, candidates are encouraged to continue monitoring the University's employment website for specific adjunct and faculty openings that match their interests and qualifications. Applying to this pool does not replace applying for individual positions when a specific vacancy is posted. Required Qualifications Master’s Degree required. A minimum of 18 hours graduate work within the coursework relevant to the specific content area is required. Experience in a post-secondary academic institution teaching non-traditional and adult students. Must be able to perform all essential duties satisfactorily. Must understand and be supportive of non-traditional students online and/or accelerated adult-focused delivery system. Must be experienced and comfortable in the online learning environment and with Brightspace learning management system. Computer expertise with MS Office is required. Good organizational and word processing skills necessary. Ability to prioritize, complete multiple tasks, and possess good interpersonal, communication, and writing skills. Attention to detail is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the SAU Concept and Community Covenant. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is our moral and legal obligation to meet the responsibility of ensuring that all management practices regarding employees are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the 1964 Civil Rights Act, and other applicable federal and state statutes, all recruiting, hiring, training, and promoting for all job classifications will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military veteran status or other applicable status protected by law, including state of employment protected classes. It is, therefore, our policy and intention to evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. All personnel related activities such as compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions and privileges of employment will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military veteran status or other applicable status protected by law, including all applicable state of employment protected classes. Spring Arbor University is a Christian religious-affiliated organization; and as such, is not subject to religious discrimination requirements; the University’s hiring practices and EEO discrimination practices are in full compliance with both federal and state law. Federal law creates an exception to the “religion” component of the employment discrimination laws for religious organizations (including educational institutions) and permits them to give employment practice preference to members of their own religious beliefs. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
