      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Bus Driver.  Bus Driver SUMMARY Spring Arbor University is accepting applications for the passenger Bus Driver position. This is a part-time, temporary position with variable hours up to 24 hours per week 11-12 months per year. RESPONSIBILITIES Driving 35, 40 and 50-passenger buses to various events, including but not limited to athletics. Includes out-of-state and overnight/weekend trips. QUALIFICATIONS CDL required MDOT Medical Certification – or will cover cost of physical at physician office contracted with SAU Candidates must have a high school diploma or equivalent Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred, and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
