    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7887a1a146071a01a14674e9501604": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician.  SUMMARY The Maintenance Technician position will have responsibilities for general maintenance and repairs for assigned facilities and equipment including, but not limited to; plumbing, electrical, basic carpentry, heating and cooling, and other building systems for SAU facilities. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES – other duties may be assigned by proper personnel. Perform general maintenance repairs – inspect, troubleshoot, and repair as needed. Conduct preventative and/or routine maintenance as needed for SAU buildings and systems. Repair and install plumbing fixtures, drain lines and other related services. Perform drain cleaning services. Assist with the management of the HVAC automation system. Cleans and assists with the upkeep of the facilities, removes trash as needed. Assist with the moving of SAU office furniture, office equipment as needed. Communicates the need for supplies and materials to supervisor. Responsible for painting projects, as assigned. Ability to repair windows and screens. Perform building walkthroughs and documentation of temperatures and pressures. Responsible for drywall maintenance. Provide routine maintenance of electrical systems and equipment. Assist with snow removal, as needed. On-call as scheduled monthly by supervisor. Performs other related duties/services as assigned. REPORTING RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as a member of facilities team reporting directly to the Director of Physical Plant. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES None QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated ability to diagnose and troubleshoot electrical issues. Ability to read and understand technical manuals and drawings/blueprints. Demonstrated ability to diagnose and troubleshoot maintenance repairs. Knowledge of general carpentry and repair. Ability to follow instructions from supervisors or lead maintenance workers. Experience and knowledge of the use of hand, power and electrical tools. Operation of motor vehicles and machinery needed to perform job duties. Maintain needed certificates for the use of chemical products or specific job-related tasks. Excellent time management skills. Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. Maintain the required license to operate a motor vehicle. Must be able to always work in a professional manner, often quietly, in a professional environment. Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Three years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience, preferred. PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to use small and large hand tools. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee must regularly lift and/or move up to 25 pounds, frequently lift and/or move up to 50 pounds, and occasionally lift and/or move up to 100 pounds with assistance. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. The employee occasionally works near moving mechanical parts and in high, precarious places and is occasionally exposed to wet and/or humid conditions, fumes or airborne particles, toxic or caustic chemicals, extreme cold, and extreme heat. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate. The employee will be required to maintain a proper state license to operate motor vehicles. While performing the duties of this job, the employee frequently works in outside weather conditions. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859fa064222601a06db52a2376d5": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician - part-time",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician - part-time.  Maintenance Technician SUMMARY Provide general maintenance services as necessary. Part time position, 25-29 hours per week. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following. Other duties may be assigned by proper personnel. General maintenance repairs Knowledge of basic plumbing projects Window, screen repairs Preventative maintenance Troubleshooting Mechanical issues around campus Changing/converting light bulbs and/or fixtures Troubleshoot electrical issues Proficient in painting Proficient in drywall maintenance Changing filters and belts as needed Building walkthrough and documentation of building temps and pressures On-call as scheduled monthly Ability to learn and apply what is needed to successfully maintain campus mechanicals Assist with snow removal and other services as needed Must be able to work quietly in professional environments Must be a team player and work well with others to resolve campus wide issues REPORTING RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as a member of business affairs reporting directly to the Director of Physical Plant. Other duties as assigned by proper personnel. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Three years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to use small and large hand tools. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee must regularly lift and/or move up to 25 pounds, frequently lift and/or move up to 50 pounds, and occasionally lift and/or move up to 100 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. While performing the duties of this job, the employee frequently works in outside weather conditions. The employee occasionally works near moving mechanical parts and in high, precarious places and is occasionally exposed to wet and/or humid conditions, fumes or airborne particles, toxic or caustic chemicals, extreme cold, and extreme heat. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate. Experience working in multicultural academic environments preferred and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a0822611be776c": {
      "title": "Academic Support Center Student Worker",
      "description": "Academic Support Center Student Worker.  Peer Tutor Peer Tutors provide academic support to fellow students through individual or small-group tutoring sessions. Tutors should have strong academic performance in the course(s) they tutor and be able to communicate course material clearly and effectively. Qualifications: Strong academic performance Faculty recommendation Dependable and responsible Strong communication skills Students interested in tutoring may contact the Academic Support Center to learn more and complete an application, which includes a faculty recommendation. Note-Taker Note-Takers provide clear and organized class notes for students with approved note-taking accommodations. Note-Takers must attend class regularly and submit notes according to Academic Support Center guidelines. Qualifications: Strong academic performance Reliable class attendance Organized and thorough note-taking skills Dependable and responsible The Academic Support Center may reach out directly to students when a Note-Taker is needed for one of their current courses. Students interested in becoming a Note-Taker may also contact the Center to be added to the list of potential Note-Takers. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a04a0aefe25cf8": {
      "title": "Ada's Kitchen Student Worker",
      "description": "Ada's Kitchen Student Worker.  Position Summary: Ada’s Kitchen is a student-run food concept located in the Poling/Walker Lounge. Student Workers support daily operations, customer service, mobile service shifts in the MAC, and overall hospitality for campus guests. This role provides hands-on experience in entrepreneurship, food service operations, marketing, and customer engagement. Key Responsibilities: • Prepare and serve grab-and-go food and beverage items according to Ada’s standards • Provide friendly, efficient customer service to students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors • Handle cash/Point-of-Sale transactions accurately and responsibly • Assist with mobile service operations in the MAC as scheduled • Maintain cleanliness of workspace, equipment, and service areas • Restock inventory and communicate low-stock needs to manager • Support special events, promotional days, or pop-up service as needed • Follow all food safety, health, and sanitation guidelines • Work collaboratively with other student employees to ensure smooth daily operations Qualifications: • Must be a current Spring Arbor University student in good academic standing • Reliable, punctual, and able to work assigned shifts independently • Strong communication skills and a customer-focused mindset • Ability to multitask and perform in a fast-paced environment • Previous food service experience helpful but not required (training provided) Learning Outcomes / Experience Gained: • Hands-on training in entrepreneurship and small-business operations • Customer service and point-of-sale experience • Event support and mobile service experience • Teamwork, communication, and problem-solving skills Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859f9fd3baa0019ff11e32de51b5": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Student Worker",
      "description": "Campus Safety Student Worker.  The Campus Safety Department is seeking alert, dependable students who are interested in helping maintain a safe campus environment. This position is a great opportunity for students interested in law, public safety, corrections, criminal justice, or related fields. Your schedule will be set and you will have consistent shifts/ hours. This position offers higher-than-average student pay. Hours: Evening, overnight, and weekend shifts are available based on departmental needs. Responsibilities: Assist Campus Safety staff with monitoring campus and reporting safety concerns. Unlock and lock campus buildings as assigned. Monitor and enforce campus parking policies. Answer phones and assist with general Campus Safety needs. Serve as an extra set of eyes and ears for the Campus Safety Department. Communicate concerns or unusual activity to Campus Safety staff. Complete other duties as assigned. Required Skills: Alert, responsible, and safety-minded. Able to remain attentive during assigned shifts. Good communication and customer service skills. Ability to follow procedures and respond appropriately to situations. Dependable and able to work independently. Qualifications: Willingness to work evening, overnight, and weekend shifts, including shifts between 4:00 p.m. and 8:00 a.m. Interest in public safety, law enforcement, criminal justice, or a related field is helpful but not required. No prior experience required; training is provided. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b019fdd048969661e": {
      "title": "Custodial Student Worker",
      "description": "Custodial Student Worker.  Shifts: Students may work early morning shifts (typically 6:00–8:00 a.m., with flexibility to leave at 7:30 a.m. for a 7:45 a.m. class) or other shifts that fit their class schedule, including residence hall assignments. Responsibilities: Clean classrooms, offices, residence halls, and other campus facilities as assigned. Vacuum, sweep, mop, dust, and sanitize designated areas. Empty trash and recycling receptacles. Clean hard surfaces and assist with general custodial tasks. Report maintenance or safety concerns to supervisors. Complete additional cleaning and maintenance duties as assigned. Required Skills: Strong work ethic and reliability. Ability to work efficiently and stay focused on assigned tasks. Attention to detail and commitment to maintaining a clean environment. Ability to work independently and follow directions. Qualifications: Ability to stand, walk, bend, and perform physical work throughout a shift. Ability to lift and carry cleaning supplies and equipment as needed. No prior custodial experience required; training is provided. Type of Work: Help maintain a clean, safe, and welcoming campus environment by performing routine custodial duties in academic buildings and residence halls. Typical duties include cleaning, vacuuming, sweeping, mopping, dusting, sanitizing surfaces, and removing trash. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883a89f8b945d019fa944557e6eff": {
      "title": "eLearning Student Worker",
      "description": "eLearning Student Worker.  eLearning ensures a standard look and feel in all SAU online and blended courses. Student workers will assist the eLearning team in maintaining quality within courses in Brightspace, the learning management system (LMS). Students will be trained to add content, check hyperlinks and courses to ensure accuracy, and assist in special projects to support the eLearning team. In addition, students may be asked to perform additional tasks as needed. Majors: Business, Communications, Professional Writing, Engineering, others as applicable Hours: Flexible hours available, Monday – Friday 9 am to 4:30 pm Required Skills: · Strong attention to detail · Effective written and verbal communication skills · High level of time management skills, attention to detail · Able to closely follow directions, refer to established documentation, and ask questions when necessary · Drive to take initiative and complete projects within established guidelines · Ability to analyze problems and apply critical thinking techniques · Ability to work in a team-oriented, collaborative environment · Ability to closely proofread for spelling and grammatical errors Technical Skills: · Experience with Brightspace learning management system and/or experience taking an online course · Familiar with Box, Google Drive, or other cloud-based file management system · Ability to comfortably use Microsoft Office 365 · Experience with digital asset creation/editing tools (Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, etc.) a plus. · Comfortable using generative artificial intelligence (AI) to streamline repetitive tasks when directed. · High comfort level with internet search and navigation Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839fa146075701a1467aa757152d": {
      "title": "English Department Student Worker",
      "description": "English Department Student Worker.  Hours: 2 to 3 hours per week Position Summary: Support departmental activities and provide service to English majors and minors. Job Responsibilities: Assist with planning department events. Update the English Department bulletin board. Communicate with current students and alumni. Update, edit, print, and scan documents. Research other English departments. Research opportunities for English students, including conferences, jobs, internships, publishing, and graduate programs. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7885ac9f8b9423019fa93b1ebd44da": {
      "title": "Food Service - Student Worker",
      "description": "Food Service - Student Worker.  Main Kitchen Students working in the Main Kitchen help support daily meal service by: Monitoring serving lines and communicating with cooks about food levels and product needs Serving food to customers in a friendly and timely manner Restocking stations throughout the shift Assisting with station cleanup, dishwashing, and general kitchen cleaning Following food safety and sanitation procedures Assisting with basic food preparation as directed Available Shifts: 4:00 p.m. – 8:30 p.m. Cougar Market Students working in the Cougar Market help provide quality customer service through: Preparing and completing customer orders Operating the point-of-sale system for meal plan swipes and credit card transactions Assisting with minor food preparation Restocking products and maintaining a clean work area Completing station cleanup and dishwashing as needed Communicating with supervisors and team members to ensure smooth operations Available Shifts: Weekends 5 p.m. – 10:30 p.m. Requirements Reliable, punctual, and able to follow instructions Able to stand for extended periods and lift up to 25 pounds No prior experience required; training is provided Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883a89f8b945d019fa94005d56d1d": {
      "title": "Gameday Staff (Men's Soccer, Men's and Women's Volleyball) Student Worker",
      "description": "Gameday Staff (Men's Soccer, Men's and Women's Volleyball) Student Worker.  Responsibilities: Assist with game-day operations for home athletic events, including men's and women's soccer, volleyball, and basketball. Welcome guests and provide excellent customer service. Perform assigned event duties to help ensure games run smoothly. Follow instructions from Athletics staff and event supervisors. Required Skills: Friendly and professional customer service skills. Dependable and punctual. Ability to communicate effectively with supervisors and guests. Ability to work as part of a team. Willingness to work evenings and weekends based on the athletic schedule. Qualifications: Ability to stand or sit for extended periods depending on the assigned role. Ability to work in both indoor and outdoor environments. No prior experience required; training is provided. Type of Work: Ticket Taker Arrive one hour before the start of each home game. Welcome spectators, collect admission payments, and assist guests entering the venue. Volleyball Ball Shagger Retrieve and return volleyballs during play. Roll balls between ball shaggers and provide the ball to the server when needed. Remain attentive throughout the match to support game officials and players. Soccer Ball Shagger Stand along the sideline throughout the game. Retrieve balls that leave the field and quickly return them to play by throwing them in as directed. Move up and down the sideline as needed during the match. Basketball Floor Crew Monitor the playing surface during the game. Mop the court as needed when moisture creates a slippery playing surface. Be prepared to respond quickly while remaining seated between assignments. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883a89f8b945d019faf87805764b2": {
      "title": "Graphic Design Student Worker",
      "description": "Graphic Design Student Worker.  SUMMARY: The Graphic Design Student Worker will prepare a student to work professionally as a graphic designer in a corporate setting. The student worker will directly assist the efforts of SAU’s Marketing & Communications office. Serving as an extension of the Visual Designer, this student will produce print and digital materials for the university. The Graphic Design Student Worker will work to find opportunities to promote and tell Spring Arbor University’s story in ways that connect departments across campus with diverse audiences, including students, prospective students, alumni, faculty and staff, donors, and friends of the university. RESPONSIBILITIES AND ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Assist with the creation of digital and print materials. Assist with projects for multiple departments across campus, including, but not limited to, Admissions, Advancement, and Student Development. Collaborate with the Visual Designer to complete projects and brainstorm ideas that align with the university’s brand guidelines. Communicate and collaborate with the team using Asana, the team’s project management system. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: An ideal candidate should know general marketing and communications practices through classes or previous work experience. Familiarity with Adobe programs such as InDesign, Photoshop, and Illustrator is preferred. The student must be able to prioritize and complete multiple tasks, possess good interpersonal and communication skills, and be creative. Students in this position must have excellent organizational skills. The ideal student worker must be able to work with little supervision, have attention to detail, complete assignments promptly, and take pride in their work. The individual will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept and Community Covenant. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78859f9fd3baa0019ff116e1094d99": {
      "title": "Grounds & Maintenance Student Worker",
      "description": "Grounds & Maintenance Student Worker.  If you enjoy working outdoors, staying active, and learning practical skills, the Grounds & Maintenance Department is a great place to work. You will work alongside the Grounds & Maintenance crew while gaining hands-on experience in landscaping, maintenance, equipment operation, and other campus projects. Hours: Students typically work 10–12 hours per week between 6:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. The department offers flexible scheduling within these hours, allowing students to arrange their work schedule around their classes and other commitments. Students may also split their hours into multiple work periods throughout the day when needed. Type of Work: Weed trimming and general landscaping. Trimming shrubs and trees. Repairing and maintaining irrigation systems. Installing landscape edging and ground cover. Assisting with sports field repair and maintenance. Operating and performing basic maintenance on small engines and equipment. Performing minor building maintenance. Assisting with office and equipment relocations. Helping with other grounds, maintenance, and campus projects as needed. Qualifications: Dependable and willing to work as part of a team. Able to work outdoors and perform physical tasks. Willing to learn and follow instructions. No prior grounds or maintenance experience required. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839fa064212401a067acf15841aa": {
      "title": "Home.FM Host - Student Worker",
      "description": "Home.FM Host - Student Worker.  Description: As a host on HOME.fm, Spring Arbor University's radio station, you will be one of the premier voices on our campus and in our community! This role is for students interested in DJing and hosting a live talk show, and students specializing in news/sports/weather roles. Hours: 5-10 per week This position includes but is not limited to: Creating podcasts & radio broadcasts, interviewing students and community members, and participating in HOME.fm’s on-campus multimedia projects. Representing HOME.fm to the student body, including participating in on-campus events as needed, making and fostering community connections, and being part of a 24-hour campus media ecosystem. Shooting and editing shortform content for social media. Engaging with followers and listeners to answer questions, give away prizes, and grow our brand. Keeping the community updated by providing correct, timely information to the public. Committing to incremental improvement, regular reviews, and striving for excellence as a student and as an employee. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7887aca03fc2d201a063714b0d3666": {
      "title": "Home.FM Producer - Student Worker",
      "description": "Home.FM Producer - Student Worker.  Description: Producers record audio & video content, edit for approval, and distribute it to our community as directed. They are, simply put, the technical expertise behind what we do, and this role represents an opportunity to work alongside SAU professionals and real clients. Each producer has a specific podcast or content specialty and is responsible for the continuity of their own project over the course of a semester. Hours: 5-10 per week This role includes but is not limited to: Using the *Adobe Suite to edit audio and video content for HOME.fm Using a live camera switcher to record video podcasts & other longform discussions inside the HOME.fm studio. Use YouTube and Podbean to distribute content according to SAU’s guidelines. Assisting your peers in creating content that is educational and representative of the university’s values. Identifying the needs of HOME.fm’s business clients and bringing ideas to address them. Engaging with followers and listeners to answer questions, give away prizes, and grow our brand. Committing to incremental improvement, regular reviews, and striving for excellence as a student and as an employee. *DaVinci Resolve is an excellent free editor if you are unable to use the Adobe Suite. However, all projects must be compatible with current Adobe formats. Transportation is preferred but not mandatory. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839fa064212401a067af6f424297": {
      "title": "Home.FM Street Team - Student Worker",
      "description": "Home.FM Street Team - Student Worker.  Description: The Street Team represents HOME.fm’s promotional, sales, and marketing efforts at Spring Arbor University. As a member of Street Team, you will produce content, participate in broadcasts, and champion the HOME.fm brand on campus. While most of our work serves our radio station, we also serve as a connector between the Spring Arbor community, advertisers, and our student body. If you are someone who loves making connections and wants to gain multimedia experience, we encourage you to apply. Hours: 5-10 per week This role includes but is not limited to: Representing HOME.fm to the student body and the larger community by participating in fundraising, networking, and promotional events. Identifying the needs of HOME.fm’s business clients and bringing ideas to address them. Helping manage the suite of HOME.fm social/web accounts. Shooting and editing shortform content for social media. Engaging with followers and listeners to answer questions, give away prizes, and grow our brand. Committing to incremental improvement, regular reviews, and striving for excellence as a student and as an employee. Transportation is preferred but not mandatory. Sales experience also appreciated Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883a89f8b945d019fa96240a57bdb": {
      "title": "Nursing Lab Student Worker",
      "description": "Nursing Lab Student Worker.  Position Summary Assist with administrative, organizational, and operational tasks supporting student success programs, faculty, and department activities. Key Responsibilities Process, scan, organize, and save student records and applicant files in Box while maintaining confidentiality. Update class lists, spreadsheets, and tracking documents related to applicants, orders, and compliance requirements. Communicate updates to faculty and student support staff as needed. Send announcements through Brightspace and maintain bulletin boards. Assist lab faculty with simulation cleanup, organizing materials, preparing labels, and restocking supplies. Prepare correspondence, form letters, and materials for student events, pinning ceremonies, and commencement. Organize and maintain digital files, including identifying and removing duplicate documents. Assist with general office duties, including copying, laminating, running errands, processing orders, and maintaining office supplies. Research items for purchase and assist with unpacking and organizing deliveries. Complete other administrative and departmental tasks as assigned. Qualifications and Expectations Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Accurate data entry and recordkeeping abilities. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and manage time effectively. Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling student records and sensitive information. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7883aca184742f01a1ac53de307410": {
      "title": "Package Delivery Student Worker",
      "description": "Package Delivery Student Worker.  Schedule: Approximately 1.5 hours each morning, with flexibility to accommodate class and athletic schedules. Position Summary: Seeking a dependable and punctual student worker to assist with daily package deliveries across campus beginning Spring 2027. This position requires morning availability and approximately 1.5 hours of work per day. Scheduling flexibility is available to accommodate class schedules and athletic commitments, including the possibility of an interrupted shift. Responsibilities: Deliver packages to designated locations across campus using a university van. Complete daily morning delivery routes in a timely and reliable manner. Handle and transport packages safely. Maintain professionalism and dependability while completing assigned deliveries. Qualifications: Must be dependable, punctual, and consistent with attendance. Must be available to work mornings. Must be able to lift and carry 50+ pounds. Must be comfortable working outdoors in various weather conditions. Must be able to operate a university van. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78839ea0f4259801a111b9c3fe2789": {
      "title": "Student Presidential Ambassador",
      "description": "Student Presidential Ambassador.  Position Summary: The Presidential Ambassador serves as a representative of the University at special events and programs hosted or supported by the Office of the President. Ambassadors help create a welcoming and professional experience for guests, students, families, alumni, donors, and other members of the University community. Responsibilities: Serve as a welcoming and professional representative of the University and the Office of the President. Assist with guest check-in, registration, seating, directions, and general event support. Welcome and interact with guests in a friendly and professional manner. Assist with event setup and cleanup as needed. Help ensure events run smoothly by responding to guest questions and providing general assistance. Assist with special activities, ceremonies, receptions, dinners, and other University events. Follow instructions provided by event coordinators and University leadership. Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor while representing the University. Perform other event-related duties as assigned. Work Schedule: Hours will vary based on the University's event schedule. Work may include daytime, evening, and weekend events throughout the academic year. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a7887a1a064211201a0922798d52b6a": {
      "title": "Video Lab Assistant Student Worker",
      "description": "Video Lab Assistant Student Worker.  Responsibilities Check out and check in video equipment for students enrolled in VID 202, VID 306, and VID 410. Inspect, clean, maintain, and secure gear housed in the video equipment cabinet. Conduct regular inventory audits of all production gear and accessories. Oversee and manage the reservation schedule for the Studio B production space. Maintain cleanliness, order, and organization across production facilities (SDH 204 and SDH 202). Participate in professional development activities to stay current on campus video gear and operational workflows. Serve as part of the Commencement livestream production team each semester (setup, cable management, and live camera operation). Execute special projects and administrative tasks as assigned by the supervisors. Required Skills Strong organizational skills and attention to detail for inventory and scheduling tasks. Reliable verbal communication and problem-solving skills when assisting students. Familiarity with basic video production equipment (e.g., DSLRs/cinema cameras, tripods, lighting, audio gear, and accessories). Basic technical troubleshooting skills for camera and production gear. Ability to follow facility safety protocols and handle fragile, high-value gear responsibly. Qualifications Current university student in good academic standing. Preference given to students who have completed or are currently enrolled in VID/media production courses. Ability to commit to 5–6 additional hours during Commencement week each semester. Availability to work scheduled shifts in the lab, including potentially variable hours. Capability to lift and transport production equipment safely (up to 25–30 lbs). Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ee9a5cc016ef0ea2d5b06cb&id=8a78879e9520a6b40195440d16f84cd0": {
      "title": "External Volunteer Application",
      "description": "External Volunteer Application.  External Volunteer Application Thank you for your interest in volunteering with Spring Arbor University. Volunteers play a vital role in the delivery of our operation, programs and events. All volunteer applications are reviewed with consideration of current volunteer opportunities. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list "
    }
  },
